  "assessment_rules": "To pass the subject, a minimum of 5 points out of 10 in the overall qualification is required. In the first ordinary call, the overall qualification is obtained from 40% continuous assessment (two tests, 20% each) and 60% final exam; no minimum mark is required for either part, and continuous assessment activities are not recoverable. In the second ordinary call and the extraordinary call for completion of studies, the final qualification is based solely on a 100% final exam, which includes all content (both continuous assessment and final exam material from the first call). Students are considered 'presented' if they participate in at least one continuous assessment test or the final exam in the first call, or if they take the final exam in other calls.",
